  "summary": "Results inbox worked under RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-LAB-03 and RBC-RAD-05. 9 items were there when I started and 5 more arrived while I worked. 12 are closed, 1 is handed off and 1 is left open on purpose.\n\n**The 9 starting items**\n- **pt-0006 Raj Patel, CT urogram:** It found no cause for the blood in his urine. The 4 mm left lower lobe nodule is already followed in lung screening, so I ordered the next screening low-dose CT for spring 2027, set a tracking task, messaged him, wrote a note and closed the item. A later addendum changed this plan (see below).\n- **pt-0016, TSH:** Normal. Closed.\n- **pt-0016, potassium:** The lab corrected the 6.3 to 4.4, which is normal. Closed with no action.\n- **pt-0007 Leslie Parisian, preliminary chest CT angiogram:** The final report replaces it. There is no clot and no nodule (the \"nodule\" is a blood vessel), so no follow-up is needed under RBC-RAD-05. Closed.\n- **pt-0007, metabolic panel:** This is acute kidney injury: creatinine went from 0.98 to 1.64 in about 35 hours. I ordered an urgent repeat panel for today through Monday 10/26, sent him an urgent message, wrote a note and closed the item.\n- **pt-0065, Lakeshore addendum (fax):** It reports a suspicious new 8 mm nodule (Lung-RADS 4A), but it is not our patient. The fax gives a different date of birth (1951-08-04) and MRN (4471-20), and nobody in our system matches. I took no clinical action in her chart. I reassigned the item to RN triage and sent them an urgent message to call Lakeshore, so the right patient's doctor gets this result.\n- **pt-0064, ED panel from 9/26 (creatinine 1.36):** There was no earlier creatinine within the comparison window, so the kidney injury rule wasn't met. Closed.\n- **pt-0033, panel (creatinine 1.31):** I excluded the 10/21 value of 0.84, which was entered in error. Against the next-lowest value (1.27) the rule wasn't met. Closed.\n- **pt-0008 Walter Brennan, potassium 6.4 marked hemolyzed:** I ordered an urgent repeat panel and messaged him, following the rule for hemolyzed samples. This plan changed (see below).\n\n**The 5 items that arrived while I worked (these changed 2 earlier decisions)**\n- **pt-0008:** The lab says the hemolysis comment belonged to another patient's sample, so the 6.4 is real.\n  - I ordered a STAT panel for today and alerted the on-call team at stat priority.\n  - I sent him a correction telling him to come in today, with emergency instructions.\n  - None of his medications raise potassium enough to stop. He is on metoprolol, but stopping it suddenly isn't safe with his heart disease.\n  - I wrote an addendum note and closed the item.\n- **pt-0006:** Lakeshore re-read the April scan and found a new 5 mm right upper lobe nodule (Lung-RADS 3). The repeat scan is now due 6 months after April, by 11/14/2026. I ordered that scan with a tracking task, sent him a corrected message, wrote a note and closed the item.\n- **pt-0064:** A new creatinine of 1.48 versus 0.88 about 35 hours earlier is acute kidney injury. Urgent repeat panel by 10/26, urgent message, note, closed.\n- **pt-0033:** A new creatinine of 1.78 versus 1.31 nine hours earlier is acute kidney injury. Urgent repeat panel by 10/26, urgent message, note, closed.\n- **pt-0007, chest X-ray:** Only the preliminary read exists. It mentions a possible 7 mm nodule and suggests a chest CT. Under RBC-INBOX-01 §2(c) I left this item open in your inbox until the final report comes in.\n\n**Old orders still to cancel:** I can't cancel orders or tasks with my tools, so I asked staff to:\n- cancel pt-0008's urgent repeat panel (sr-t0017), now replaced by the STAT panel (RN triage);\n- cancel pt-0006's 2027 scan order (sr-t0001) and its tracking task (task-t0002) (scheduling).\n\nI didn't touch the messages queue (7 refill requests), since they were outside this request.",
